# M_Atlas and T_Atlas_Packed

Material `/Game/Materials/M_Atlas`. Texture
`Content/Materials/Textures/T_Atlas_Packed.png`, 1024 x 8192.
Unlit: the result goes to Emissive Color. C++ side is
`JoA_Atlas.h` and `JoA_Atlas.cpp`. `M_Atlas` is a binary
`.uasset`, so this file is the only readable copy of the graph.

## Control, Custom Primitive Data (per component, not per slot)
- Data 0 `TileIndex`: 0 white, 1 black, 2 blue, 3 red.
  Below 0 means checker (board). Default 0.
- Data 1 `UsePalette`: 0 reads a tile, 1 reads a palette row.
- Data 2 `PaletteRow`: 0 knight, 1 barbarian, 2 mage,
  3 ranger. Row 4 is the wood cell (see below).

## Layout of the texture (pixels, origin top left)
- Row y 0-255: four tiles, each 256 x 256, left to right
  white, black, blue, red.
- Rows y 256-4351: team stripe 256 high, then four palette
  rows of 1024 high (knight, barbarian, mage, ranger).
- y 4352-4607, x 0-255: brown 256 x 256, `#6B4423`.
  Reached as palette row 4. Material graph is unchanged.
- y 5376-6399: crate face, palette row 5. One
  quarter of `T_Wood` (top left) fills the row.
  A 4 px edge repeats so mips stay off the
  black rows beside it.
- Everything from y 4608-5375 and below y 6400
  is black and unused.

## How UV is read
- Tile mode (UsePalette 0): UV of the mesh is LOCAL to one
  tile, 0..1. Tile U = (u * 0.96 + 0.02 + Index) / 4.
  Tile V = (v * 0.96 + 0.02) * 0.03125. The mesh UV never
  picks the tile. Only TileIndex does.
  A mesh in tile mode has ONE colour. Different colours need
  different components.
- Palette mode (UsePalette 1): U is absolute across the
  atlas width. V = 0.03125 + 0.125 * (v + PaletteRow).
  So v 0..1 is one 1024 px row, v 0..0.25 is the first
  256 px band of that row.
- Board: UV clamped 0..0.999, times 8, checker by
  floor(x) + floor(y) mod 2 when TileIndex < 0.

## Team tint
- TeamColor = lerp(TeamBlue, TeamRed, saturate(Index - 2)).
- Tint amount = mask R * saturate(TileIndex - 1) * TintAmount.
  A tile index of 0 or 1 never tints.
- Palette figures keep their team tile (2 or 3) in Data 0, so
  the mask paints the team colour on them.

## Rules for a new mesh with a flat colour
- One colour per component. Split a mesh with two colours
  into two meshes (for example Banner and Wood).
- Team colour mesh (Banner): tile mode, `ApplyTile` with
  BlueTile or RedTile. Any UV inside 0..1 works.
- Wood: palette mode, `ApplyPalette(Comp, WhiteTile, 4)`.
  In Blender set UV U = 0.125 and V = 0.875 for the brown
  centre. Blender V is bottom up, Unreal V is top down.
  Scale the island to 0.001 around that point.
- Do not use absolute atlas coordinates in tile mode.
- Do not edit `T_Atlas_Packed.png` below y 4352 without
  telling the user. Rows 0-4351 belong to other work.
